Count":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, 40,400","reason":"The side displacements are (2000, 200) and (2, y + 22). Perpendicularity gives 4000 + 200(y + 22) = 0, so y = -42. The side lengths are 200√101 and 2√101, giving area 400 × 101 = 40,400.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2006_AMC_10B_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_186","cnm_p089"],"id":"perpendicular-slopes","label":"Method 1: Use perpendicular slopes","methodDirectNodeIds":{"perpendicular-slopes":["cnm_h167","cnm_h168","cnm_h173"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h167","cnm_h168","cnm_h173","cnm_186","cnm_p089"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_186","cnm_p089"],"id":"right-triangle-distance-equation","label":"Method 2: Use the Pythagorean theorem","methodDirectNodeIds":{"right-triangle-distance-equation":["cnm_174","cnm_h173","cnm_148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_174","cnm_h173","cnm_148","cnm_186","cnm_p089"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 8√1003","reason":"Let the rectangle sides be u and v, so uv = 2006 and 2a = u+v. Since c² = (u²+v²)/4, b² = a²-c² = uv/2 = 1003. The ellipse area gives ab = 2006, hence a = 2√1003 and the rectangle perimeter is 4a = 8√1003.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2006_AMC_12B_Q21","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_186","cnm_p089","cnm_p078"],"id":"focal-sum-and-semiaxes","label":"Relate the rectangle sides to the ellipse axes","methodDirectNodeIds":{"focal-sum-and-semiaxes":["cnm_h183","cnm_h185","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h183","cnm_h185","cnm_174","cnm_186","cnm_p089","cnm_p078"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"48","reason":"The diagonals bisect each other, so AC = BD = 10. The rectangle has BC = sqrt(100 - 36) = 8 and area 6 × 8 = 48.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"ca